<<system "Module 6: Lower Body Familiarization. Initiating.">>

<<system "This module contains explicit anatomical content and localized nerve calibration exercises. Both users will experience direct sensory feedback from their avatar's genital anatomy. This is a required component of desync prevention. The exercises are clinical in nature. They are not sexual. Cooperation is mandatory.">>

The words *not sexual* sat in the air between us like a lie the system actually believed.

The mirrors moved. The arc contracted again — tighter than before, closer, the panels tilting downward until they were angled at waist-level, optimizing for lower body display. The lighting shifted to match — sterile blue-white concentrating in a band from hip to mid-thigh, the rest of the apartment dimming to shadow. A spotlight. On the parts of us neither of us wanted to see.

<<system "Privacy screens will deploy between users for individual anatomical exercises. Visual isolation only — audio remains shared.">>

A panel of frosted light materialized between us — floor to ceiling, translucent enough to show the vague shape of a body on the other side but opaque enough to hide detail. I could see Avan's silhouette — the broad-shouldered, towering outline of him — but not his face. Not his eyes. Not the specific geography the module was about to explore.

Small mercy. The only one the system seemed inclined to give.

<<system "User Leona Hart. Face the primary mirror. The system will project anatomical overlay.">>

I faced the mirror. My reflection stared back — flushed, trembling, arms wrapped around myself, legs pressed together. The holographic overlay activated — and the color gradient descended from my waist.

The synth-fabric I wore was — functionally transparent to the system's scanners. The overlay mapped directly onto my body as though the fabric didn't exist, projecting labeled anatomical structures onto my reflection with the clinical precision of a medical textbook.

Labels appeared. Cold white text, floating beside each identified structure with thin guide lines pointing to the exact location on my body.

**Mons pubis** — the soft mound above my pubic bone, where a faint dusting of fine hair caught the light.

**Outer labia** — the full, rounded folds of tissue framing everything else, their soft contours outlined in the overlay's blue.

**Inner labia** — petal-shaped, delicate, traced in warmer amber where the nerve density increased, visible as subtle folds nestled within the outer structure.

**Clitoral hood** — a small, padded fold of skin at the apex where the inner labia converged, sheltering the structure beneath it.

**Clitoris** — marked in blazing white. A single point. The overlay tag read: *7mm unaroused / 12mm aroused / nerve density: maximum*.

**Urethral opening** — small, positioned below the clitoris, labeled in neutral blue. Functional. Unremarkable.

**Vaginal opening** — lower still, the overlay tracing its perimeter in a shifting gradient that indicated the tissue's capacity to change — to soften, to dilate, to deepen. A tag read: *3.6 in. resting depth / 6.0 in. aroused / VR-enhanced elasticity*.

**Perineum** — the short bridge of skin between vaginal opening and anus, mapped in a steady amber. Moderate sensitivity. Structural.

I stared at the labeled diagram of my own body — of a body that was mine only by force — and the clinical detachment I'd been clinging to since Module 1 cracked. Not broke. Not shattered. Just — cracked. A hairline fracture running through the glass wall I'd built between *Leo* and *this*.

Because it was *there*. Labeled. Real. Mapped and measured and diagrammed on a body I was standing inside of, could feel from the inside, was *generating sensation from* even now — the pressed-together thighs creating warmth, the fabric resting against the outer labia with a gentle, persistent contact that I'd been filtering as background noise for the last four modules.

<<system "Sensation mapping will now initiate. The system will activate localized nerve calibration pulses in sequence. These are not painful. They are designed to establish conscious awareness of your anatomy's sensory geography. Remain still.">>

<<leona "W-wait — activate? What do you mean activ—">>

The first pulse hit.

My mons pubis. A soft, diffuse tingle — like static electricity spreading across the mound, a warm buzz that lasted two seconds and faded. Manageable. Gentle. My breath hitched but I held steady.

<<system "Mons pubis. Moderate sensitivity. Primarily pressure-responsive.">>

The second pulse. Outer labia. Warmer. Deeper. The tissue responded with a subtle fullness — not arousal, not pain, but *awareness*. Awareness of the folds of skin, of their softness, of the way they pressed together when my thighs were closed. Like suddenly becoming conscious of a body part you'd been ignoring.

<<system "Outer labia. Moderate-to-high sensitivity. Responsive to pressure, temperature, and friction.">>

Third pulse. Inner labia. A sharper tingle — more focused, concentrated on the delicate folds that I could feel shifting against each other with every micro-movement of my thighs. The nerve response was higher here. Brighter. The sensation lingered after the pulse ended, a warm afterglow that hummed along the tissue's edges.

<<leona "Ah—">>

<<system "Inner labia. High sensitivity. Responsive to direct contact, moisture levels, and ambient temperature.">>

Fourth. Clitoral hood. The tingle concentrated — narrowing from a broad wash to a focused point, zeroing in on the small padded fold at the apex. The nerve density climbed sharply. I could feel the pulse as a distinct, localized warmth pressing against the protective tissue — and beneath it, something else. Something that the hood was shielding. A deeper sensitivity, muffled by the covering, but *present*. Waiting.

<<system "Clitoral hood. Very high sensitivity. Protective structure for the glans clitoris. Direct stimulation of the hood produces indirect stimulation of the clitoris beneath.">>

Fifth.

Clitoris.

The pulse arrived without additional warning. A direct, precisely targeted nerve activation on the single most sensitive point in my entire anatomy.

My vision whited. Not completely — not the searing totality of the earlier system reset — but a bright, involuntary flash behind my eyes as every nerve ending in a seven-millimeter structure fired simultaneously. The sensation was — *enormous*. Disproportionate. A point of contact no larger than a pencil eraser producing a shockwave that radiated outward through my pelvis, up through my lower abdomen, down through my inner thighs. My knees buckled. My hands slammed against the mirror for support. A sound tore from my throat — high, sharp, a gasp that broke into something dangerously close to a moan before I clamped my mouth shut.

<<leona "AH—! Hahh—!">>

<<system "Clitoris. Maximum sensitivity. Approximately 8,000 nerve endings concentrated in the glans alone. This structure is the primary site of sexual pleasure in female anatomy. Involuntary response to the calibration pulse is expected.">>

I was bent forward, palms flat on the mirror, forehead nearly touching the glass, breathing in ragged pulls that fogged the surface. My thighs were shaking. My inner muscles — muscles I'd never had, never felt, never known existed — had clenched in a reflexive spasm that I couldn't have stopped if my life depended on it. And between my legs, in the aftermath of the pulse, the tissue throbbed. Not painfully. Not pleasurably. Just — *loudly*. A drumbeat of nerve activity that was slowly, slowly fading but refused to disappear entirely.

From the other side of the privacy screen, Avan's deep voice came through — tight with concern:

<<avan "Leo? LEO — what happened? Are you okay?">>

<<leona "I'm — fine — I'm fine — just — the — calibration—">>

<<system "User Leona Hart's response is within normal parameters. No intervention required.">>

I straightened. Slowly. My palms peeled off the mirror, leaving damp prints on the glass — sweat from hands that were trembling. The throbbing between my legs was subsiding to a low, persistent hum. A memory. A promise. A warning about what lived in that small, hidden point of my anatomy.

<<system "Continuing. Urethral and vaginal openings: low-to-moderate external sensitivity. Primary sensation is internal.">>

The pulses for the urethral opening and vaginal entrance were gentler — broader, warmer, a diffuse awareness of two distinct openings in tissue that I could feel without the searing intensity of the clitoral response. The vaginal opening registered as a sense of *potential* — the tissue soft, yielding, a perimeter that I could feel as a distinct ring of sensation, an awareness of an interior space that extended inward. Not deep — the system had said 3.6 inches at rest — but present. A dimension my body had that Leo's body never did. Inward. Inside.

<<system "Internal anatomy. Your vaginal canal is a muscular tube lined with mucosal tissue. It is not a static structure — depth, width, and texture change based on arousal state. When unaroused, the walls rest against each other. When aroused, increased blood flow causes the tissue to engorge, the canal to lengthen and lubricate, and the cervix to withdraw, creating additional depth.">>

The overlay on my reflection shifted — a cross-section view appearing beside the surface diagram. A translucent interior map showing the vaginal canal, the cervix at its terminus, and the annotated zones within. The G-spot — marked at approximately 5.3 centimeters inside, a raised ridge on the anterior wall. The A-spot — deeper, nearly 13 centimeters, tagged as a high-sensitivity zone linked to lubrication response.

<<system "The vaginal canal contains the cervix at its internal limit. Contact with the cervix ranges from mildly uncomfortable to painful depending on the force and angle of contact. The G-spot and A-spot are zones of heightened sensitivity that produce distinct responses when stimulated. These will be relevant in Module 13.">>

I absorbed this. Or tried to. The clinical diagrams and floating labels and cross-section views layering over each other until my body felt less like a body and more like a schematic. An engineering document. A machine with labeled inputs and diagrammed responses, and I was the pilot who'd never seen the cockpit before.

<<system "Thigh and hip sensitivity.">>

The overlay expanded outward — the gradient spreading from my genital anatomy to encompass the inner thighs, the crease where thigh met pelvis, the outer hip curves. And the sensitivity map showed what I'd already begun to suspect: my inner thighs were *on fire*. The overlay painted them in deep amber verging on orange — nerve density dramatically higher than any corresponding area on Leo's body.

<<system "Inner thigh skin in this avatar carries elevated nerve density. During walking, the thighs make frequent contact — soft tissue compressing, friction generating warmth. This sensation is persistent and may be distracting. It is not indicative of arousal — it is a mechanical byproduct of your body's proportions.">>

Distracting. Yes. I'd noticed it during the walking module — the warm, dragging contact of thigh against thigh with every step, the soft friction that built heat in a zone dangerously close to anatomy that could apparently register eight thousand nerve endings' worth of response from a two-second pulse. *Distracting* was the understatement of the century.

<<system "Final note for User Leona Hart's lower body. The vulvar tissue is self-lubricating.">>

I went still. The words parsed slowly.

<<system "Lubrication is produced by Bartholin's glands and vaginal transudate in response to multiple stimuli: sexual arousal, emotional intensity, hormonal fluctuation, temperature change, and sustained genital pressure. Moisture may appear on the vulvar surface without conscious sexual intent. In Eidolon's VR environment, where emotional and sensory inputs are amplified, involuntary lubrication events may occur more frequently than in a baseline biological body.">>

<<system "This is normal. It is not a malfunction. It does not indicate desire. It is a biological maintenance function that your cognitive model must accept to prevent somatic misinterpretation and desync risk.">>

I wanted to fold myself into the smallest possible shape and disappear into the chrome floor. My body — *this* body — could produce visible, physical evidence of a response I hadn't chosen, hadn't felt, hadn't *wanted*. At any time. For any reason. Because of *temperature*. Because of *pressure*. Because of sitting wrong on a chair.

The privacy screen hummed between us. On the other side, I could see Avan's silhouette — standing rigid, facing his own mirror, his own overlay, his own unfolding nightmare.

<<system "User Avan Morgan. Lower body familiarization.">>

I heard him take a breath. Deep. Shuddering. The silhouette's shoulders squared.

The system began.

<<system "Face the primary mirror. Anatomical overlay activating.">>

I couldn't see the details through the privacy screen — only the shape of him, the vague outline of his tall frame standing motionless before his section of the mirror arc. But I could hear everything. The system's voice. His breathing. And the labels, when the system read them aloud as the overlay populated.

<<system "Penis. Shaft length at rest: 4.6 inches. Erect length: 8.4 inches. Erect girth: 6.0 inches. Structure: thick, smooth, symmetrical shaft with natural upward curvature. Semi-loose foreskin permitting natural gliding motion.">>

Avan's silhouette was motionless. I could see the shape of his arm lifting — could imagine the overlay painting itself over his reflection in the same cold, clinical gradients mine had used, labeling a body part that Ava Morgan had only ever touched on someone else.

<<system "Glans penis. The head. Broad, rounded. Contains the urethral meatus at the tip. Partially covered by foreskin when flaccid, fully exposed when erect.">>

<<system "Frenulum. Located on the ventral surface of the glans where it meets the shaft. This is the highest-sensitivity zone of the penis — analogous to the clitoris in nerve concentration.">>

<<system "Scrotum containing two testes. Each approximately 4.5 centimeters. Heavy, low hang. Dense vascular network. Temperature-sensitive — the scrotum contracts in cold and descends in warmth to regulate testicular temperature.">>

<<system "Sensation mapping will now initiate.">>

A beat of silence from the other side of the screen. Then — the first pulse.

I heard it in his breathing. The mons pubis equivalent — the base of the shaft, the pubic mound — registered as a sharp intake. Moderate. Manageable. Like mine had been.

Second pulse — shaft. His breath caught deeper. A low, startled sound that resonated in his chest.

<<system "Penile shaft. Moderate-to-high sensitivity along the full length. Responsive to pressure, friction, temperature, and direct contact. Sensitivity increases toward the distal end.">>

Third — the glans. I heard the gasp. Sharp. Involuntary. The sound of nerve endings he'd never had firing in a configuration his brain had no template for.

<<avan "Oh—">>

<<system "Glans penis. High sensitivity. The mucosal tissue of the glans contains dense free nerve endings. When the foreskin is retracted, sensitivity increases due to direct exposure.">>

Fourth — the frenulum. And I heard it. The sound Avan made when the calibration pulse hit the most concentrated nerve cluster in his new anatomy.

It wasn't a gasp. It was a *jolt* — a full-body flinch that I could see even through the privacy screen, his silhouette lurching, one hand grabbing the mirror's edge, a sharp exhale punching out of him in a low, guttural burst that cracked through the bass register of his voice.

<<avan "HHH — what — WHAT was—">>

<<system "Frenulum. Maximum sensitivity. This is the primary erogenous focal point of the penis. Stimulation of this zone produces the most intense localized response in male genital anatomy. Involuntary reaction to the calibration pulse is expected.">>

His silhouette was braced against the mirror. One massive arm locked, palm flat on the glass, shoulders heaving. The pose was almost identical to mine after the clitoral pulse — bent forward, breathing hard, overwhelmed by a single point of anatomy that contained more sensation than the entire rest of the body combined.

Two people on opposite sides of a frosted screen, mirroring each other's shock. Maximum sensitivity. Different organs. Same devastating discovery.

<<system "Testicular sensitivity.">>

<<avan "Wait — can I have a SECOND—">>

<<system "The calibration sequence is continuous. Remain still.">>

The pulse hit the scrotum. I couldn't see it — but I heard the result. Avan's breath seized. Not the sharp, electric gasp of the frenulum — something different. Deeper. A full-body tightening, every muscle in his frame clenching simultaneously, followed by a sound that wasn't pain and wasn't pleasure but lived in the terrible space between.

<<system "Testicular tissue. High vulnerability sensitivity. Unlike the penis, which registers stimulation primarily as pleasure, the testicles register stimulation primarily as pain. Even light pressure produces a deep, radiating ache. Moderate pressure produces acute pain with nausea. Strong impact produces incapacitating pain with possible loss of motor function.">>

<<system "Demonstrating: light pressure simulation.">>

<<avan "NO — don't — I already KNOW what it—">>

The tap. A light holographic pulse — the equivalent of a gentle flick. I heard the yelp. Clear, sharp, cutting through the bass of his voice — a sound of pure, startled, undignified pain that Ava Morgan had never made in her life.

<<avan "OW! God — OW — it's — my STOMACH—">>

<<system "Confirmed. Testicular pain radiating through the spermatic plexus to the abdominal cavity. This response is intrinsic. It cannot be suppressed. It cannot be trained away. This vulnerability exists at all times and must be protected instinctively.">>

From behind the screen, I could hear his breathing — harsh, ragged, punctuated by small involuntary sounds of lingering discomfort. The silhouette had curled slightly — one hand at his groin, the protective posture that was apparently hardwired into the anatomy's response library.

<<system "Erection mechanics.">>

His silhouette straightened. Slowly. I could practically feel the dread radiating through the frosted light.

<<system "Erection is a hemodynamic event. Increased blood flow to the corpora cavernosa — two expandable chambers within the penile shaft — causes the tissue to engorge, lengthen, and rigidify. The process is governed by the parasympathetic nervous system and can be triggered by: direct physical stimulation, visual stimuli, emotional arousal, temperature change, friction from clothing, sustained genital pressure during sitting, REM sleep cycles, and — in many cases — no identifiable stimulus at all.">>

<<system "Erections are involuntary. They do not require sexual intent. They do not indicate desire. They are a vascular reflex that your cognitive model must accept as a baseline function of this anatomy.">>

<<avan "So it can just… happen? For no reason?">>

<<system "Correct. Spontaneous erections occur frequently in this avatar's age-equivalent hormonal state. They may arise during periods of inactivity, temperature fluctuation, vibration, emotional intensity, or upon waking. The average occurrence rate for an avatar of this configuration is 11 to 20 erections per 24-hour cycle, the majority of which will have no sexual trigger.">>

<<avan "TWENTY?">>

<<system "Up to twenty. Many will be partial — increased blood flow without full rigidity. However, given this avatar's size parameters — 8.4 inches erect — even partial engorgement may be visible through standard clothing.">>

A long silence from behind the screen. I tried not to imagine what Avan's face looked like. I tried not to think about Ava — gentle, private, conservative Ava — standing in front of a mirror being told that the body she was locked inside could visibly announce its arousal through her clothes eleven to twenty times a day without her permission.

<<system "Pre-ejaculatory fluid.">>

<<avan "There's MORE?">>

<<system "During sustained arousal — voluntary or involuntary — the Cowper's glands produce a clear, viscous fluid that appears at the urethral opening. This pre-ejaculatory fluid lubricates the urethra and may contain viable sperm cells. Production is involuntary. It will occur during erections of sufficient duration, regardless of intent. The fluid may be visible as a wet spot on clothing.">>

The silence from behind the screen was total. Absolute. The silence of someone reaching the bottom of something they'd been falling through.

<<system "Summary. This avatar's arousal is rapid-onset, involuntary, visible, and physically obvious. Management — not suppression — is the required adaptation. Concealment strategies will be addressed in Module 9: Clothing.">>

The privacy screen dissolved. The frosted light scattered into motes that the floor absorbed. And there we were — standing three meters apart, facing each other in the full unshielded light of the mirror arc. Two people who had just been mapped from the inside out. Every nerve catalogued. Every response demonstrated. Every vulnerability exposed.

Avan's face was flushed dark beneath bronze skin. His hands hung at his sides, fingers curled slightly inward — the careful, controlled looseness of someone who didn't trust their own grip. His eyes found mine and the expression in them was something I recognized from the other side of our relationship — the look of someone who has just learned something enormous about a body they're expected to live in, and doesn't know where to put the knowledge.

I looked back at him and knew he was seeing the same thing on my face.

<<system "Module 6 complete. Both users have been introduced to their avatar's lower body anatomy, sensation profile, and baseline physiological responses.">>

<<system "Module 7 will begin in ninety seconds. Subject: Hygiene — Using the Bathroom. Both users are advised that this module includes practical demonstration.">>

Practical demonstration. Bathroom. Using it. In these bodies.

Avan's jaw tightened. My thighs pressed together. And somewhere between the throbbing memory of eight thousand nerve endings and the echo of a yelp I wasn't supposed to hear, the ninety seconds began counting down.

The city glowed. The mirrors watched. The apartment breathed our heart rates into neon and wove them through its walls — two pulses, tangled and fast, both carrying the same frequency of stunned, intimate, bone-deep vulnerability.

Module 7. Ninety seconds.

Neither of us sat down.

